G0514.def:
ἄξιος, -α, -ον
(ἄγω, in sense, to weigh), [in LXX for בֵּן (Deutéronome 25:2), מָלֵא, שָׁוָה; frequently in Wis, 2Mac ;] 
__1. Part One 
__(a) of weight, worth (often with genitive, cf. Pr 315, 811), before πρός: Romains 8:18 (see Field, Notes, 157); 
__(b) befitting, meet: with genitive, Matthieu 3:8, Luc 3:8 23:41, Actes 26:20, 1 Corinthiens 16:4 (see M, Pr., 216); absol., 2 Thessaloniciens 1:3; 
__(with) of persons, worthy; 
__2. Part Two
__α in good sense: with genitive of thing(s), Matthieu 10:10, Luc 7:4 10:7, Actes 13:46, 1 Timothée 1:15 4:9 5:18 6:1; with aor. inf. (see M, Pr., 203): Luc 15:19, 21, Act_13:25, Apocalypse 4:11 5:2, 4 5:9, 12; before ἵνα: Jean 1:27; ἅς, Luc 7:4; absol., but of what understood: Matthieu 10:11, 13 22:8, Apocalypse 3:4; with genitive of person(s), Matthieu 10:37-38, Hébreux 11:38; 
__β in bad sense; with genitive of thing(s), Luc 12:48 23:15, Actes 23:29 25:11, 25 26:31, Romains 1:32; absol., Apocalypse 16:6 (MM, VGT, see word).†

G0563.def:
ἀπεριστπάστως 
adv. (περισπάω the adj. occurs in Wis.16:11 Sir.41:1); 
without distraction: 1 Corinthiens 7:35.†

G0565.def:
ἀπέρχομαι, 
[in LXX chiefly for הלךְ ;] 
__1. to go away, depart (also, in late writers, with "perfective" force, to arrive at a destination, the thought being carried on to the goal; M, Pr., 111f., 247; MM, see word); 
__(a) absol.: Matthieu 13:25, al.; ptcp., ἀπελθών, used pleonastically with other verbs as in Heb. (Dalman, Words, 21), Matthieu 13:28, al.; 
__(b) with mention of place or person: εἰς, Matthieu 14:15; ἐπί, Luc 24:24; πρός, Apocalypse 10:9; ἀπό, Luc 1:38; ἐξω, Actes 4:15; ἐκεῖ, Matthieu 2:22. 
__2. As in LXX, before ὀπίσω, with genitive (Heb. הָלַךְ אַחֲרֵי), to go after, follow: Marc 1:20, Jean 12:19; metaphorically, Marc 1:42, Apocalypse 21:1.

G0575.def:
ἀπό (on the frequently neglect of elision bef. vowels, see Tdf., Pr., 94, WH, App., 146), 
prep. with genitive (WM, 462ff.; on its relation to ἐκ, παρά, ὑπό, ib. 456f.), [in LXX for לְ ,בְּ ,מִן ;] 
from (i.e. from the exterior). 
__1. Of separation and cessation; 
__(1) of motion from a place: Matthieu 5:29, 30 7:23, Luc 5:2 22:41, al.; 
__(2) in partitive sense (M, Pr., 72, 102, 245; MM, see word; Bl., §40, 2), Matthieu 9:16 27:21, Jean 21:10, Actes 5:2, al.; also after verbs of eating, etc.; 
__(3) of alienation (cl. genitive of separation), after such verbs as λούω (Deiss., BS, 227), λύω, σώζω, παύω, etc.; ἀνάθεμα ἀ., Romains 9:3; ἀποθνήσκειν ἀ., Colossiens 2:20; σαλευθῆναι, 2 Thessaloniciens 2:2, καθαρός, -ίζειν, ἀ. (Deiss., BS, 196, 216), Actes 20:26, 2 Corinthiens 7:1, Hébreux 9:14; 
__(4) of position, Matthieu 23:34 24:31, al.; after μακράν, Matthieu 8:30; transposed before measures of distance, Jean 10:18 21:8, Apocalypse 14:20 (Abbott, JG, 227); 
__(5) of time, ἀπὸ τ. ὥρας, ἡμέρας, etc., Matthieu 9:22, Jean 19:27, Actes 20:18, Philippiens 1:5, al.; ἀπ᾽ αἰῶνος, Luc 1:70, al.; ἀπ᾽ ἀρχῆς, etc., Matthieu 19:4, Romains 1:20; ἀπὸ βρέφους, 2 Timothée 3:15; ἀφ᾽ ἧς, since, Luc 7:45, al.; ἀπὸ τ. νῦν, Luc 1:48, al.; ἀπὸ τότε, Matthieu 4:17, al.; ἀπὸ πέρυσι, a year ago, 2 Corinthiens 8:10 9:2; ἀπὸ πρωΐ, Actes 28:23; 
__(6) of order or rank, ἀπὸ διετοῦς, Matthieu 2:16; ἀπὸ Ἀβραάμ, Matthieu 1:17; ἐβδομος ἀπὸ Ἀδάμ, Ju 14; ἀπὸ μικροῦ ἕως μεγάλου, Actes 8:10, Hébreux 8:11; ἄρχεσθαι ἀπό, Matthieu 20:8, Jean 8:9, Actes 8:35, al. 
__2. Of origin; 
__(1) of birth, extraction, and hence, in late writers, 
__(a) of local extraction (cl. ἐξ; Abbott, JG, 227ff.), Matthieu 21:11, Marc 15:43, Jean 1:45, Actes 10:38, al.; οἱ ἀπὸ Ἰταλίας (WM, §66, 6; M, Pr., 237; Westc, Rendall, in l.), Hébreux 13:24; 
__(b) of membership in a community or society (BL, §40, 2), Actes 12:1, al.; 
__(with) of material (= cl. genitive; Bl. l.with; M, Pr., 102), Matthieu 3:4 27:21; 
__(d) after verbs of asking, seeking, etc., Luc 11:50, 51 1 Thessaloniciens 2:6 (Milligan, in l.); 
__(2) of the cause, instrument, means or occasion (frequently = ὑπό, παρά, and after verbs of learning, hearing, knowing, etc.; Bl., §40, 3), Matthieu 7:16 11:29, Luc 22:45, Actes 2:22 4:36 9:13 12:14, 1 Corinthiens 11:23, Galates 3:2, al.; ἀπὸ τ. ὄχλου, Luc 19:3 (cf. Jean 21:6, Actes 22:11); ἀπὸ τ. φόβου, Matthieu 14:26, al. (cf. Matthieu 10:26 13:44). 
__3. Noteworthy Hellenistic phrases: φοβεῖσθαι ἀπό (M, Pr., 102, 107); προσέχειν ἀπό (M, Pr., 11. with; Milligan, NTD, 50); ἀπὸ νότου (Heb. מִגֶּנֶב), Apocalypse 21:13; ἀπὸ προσώπου (מִפְּנֵי), 2 Thessaloniciens 1:9 (Bl., §40, 9); ἀπὸ τ. καρδιῶν (בְּלֵב), Matthieu 18:35; ἀπὸ ὁ ὤν (WM, §10, 2; M, Pr., 9), Apocalypse 1:4. 
__4. In composition, ἀπό denotes separation, departure, origin, etc. (ἀπολύω, ἀπέρχομαι, ἀπογράφω); it also has a perfective force (M, Pr., 112, 247), as in ἀφικνεῖσθαι, which see
